From a497d4e53160921777408aa6623ba74437822777 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 22:29:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 28/91] moe-stream : runahead (G2) - at decode the remap of a
 layer is split in two, and between the halves the next layer's experts are
 predicted from an approximate pass over the resident ones

LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_RUNAHEAD=K (0 = off, the default). The first half (llama_moe_stream_remap_issue) does what the remap
does up to its wait - count, trace, classify, reserve and queue the call's loads - and returns at once with the slots
of the experts resident when the call came; a pair whose expert is not gets a resident slot of its token (or of the
layer) at weight 0 (llama_moe_stream_drop_mask). Those slots are kept and fenced. On the GPU the graph then computes
FFN L from them plus the shared expert (computed once, reused by the exact sum), carries the hyper-connection streams
into L+1, runs L+1's attention (its cache writes are written again by the real attention before anything reads them;
off with rollback snapshots, n_rs_seq > 0) and L+1's router. The second half (llama_moe_stream_remap_wait) stages the
top K of that prediction into L+1 through predict_locked and the stage dispatcher, waits for L's loads and hands the
exact expert GEMMs their slots. The exact layer is unchanged: text = trace.

Two fixes on the way:
- llama-context: resolve_fused_ops skips a fused node that is not in the graph. A dead fused node (built, consumed by
  nothing) has no backend, counted as a device mismatch, and turned the fused DSV4 hc comb off for the whole graph;
  the non-fused comb moved the output by KL 0.006.
- the pass collapses FFN L+1's input with the carried mix instead of building FFN L+1's own mix, whose post and comb
  were those dead nodes.
- graph_max_nodes doubles while runahead is on.

LLAMA_MOE_STREAM_RA_DEBUG (bits) are the measurement modes that located the dead node.

SiegeLadder runs.md 4.42: main mode (46 GiB, PASSIVE), first run 13.45 tok/s against 12.34 without, text = trace;
the prediction caught ~91% of the misses with ~0.1 false guesses per call.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
